01:20:58.936 --> 01:20:59.769
(the rest laugh)

01:20:59.769 --> 01:21:00.602
And then she spoke

01:21:00.602 --> 01:21:02.866
in crew disgusting
virus-spreading English.

01:21:02.866 --> 01:21:03.927
(the rest laugh)
She says,

01:21:03.927 --> 01:21:05.033
"this is a pen"

01:21:06.030 --> 01:21:08.430
and the spit went everywhere,
the virus went everywhere.

01:21:08.430 --> 01:21:10.000
It was conclusive evidence.

01:21:10.000 --> 01:21:11.080
The English language was--

01:21:11.080 --> 01:21:13.977
- That's why the virus is more viral.

01:21:13.977 --> 01:21:16.060
- It wasn't an absence of mass testing,

01:21:16.060 --> 01:21:17.980
or the widespread use of masks.

01:21:17.980 --> 01:21:19.570
It was (speaks in foreign language),

01:21:19.570 --> 01:21:21.843
British people, Americans speaking.

01:21:22.870 --> 01:21:25.950
- I made a sarcastic tweet
after I saw that clip--

01:21:25.950 --> 01:21:26.783
- I was so frustrated.

01:21:26.783 --> 01:21:28.360
- Where I retweeted it and said like,

01:21:28.360 --> 01:21:29.940
because every foreigner in Japan goes

01:21:29.940 --> 01:21:31.268
around asking what a pen is.

01:21:31.268 --> 01:21:32.420
- (laughs) Exactly, right?

01:21:32.420 --> 01:21:33.720
- Speak for yourself Joey.

01:21:35.010 --> 01:21:35.843
- Is this a pen?

01:21:37.429 --> 01:21:39.547
- (speaks in a foreign language)

01:21:39.547 --> 01:21:42.130
- Is that a pen?
- Is that a pen?

01:21:42.130 --> 01:21:44.950
- So that was like, okay,
I'm doing this video now.

01:21:44.950 --> 01:21:47.070
I've wanted it for years
and I'm doing it now.

01:21:47.070 --> 01:21:49.694
That is the catalyst, so
that was my main driver to do

01:21:49.694 --> 01:21:50.970
a video on why I hate Japanese TV,

01:21:50.970 --> 01:21:52.990
and talk about my experiences
being on TV for me.

01:21:52.990 --> 01:21:55.090
- It's a shame for me, as well,

01:21:55.090 --> 01:21:59.050
because like I said in
episode three that like,

01:21:59.050 --> 01:22:00.330
a lot of my Japanese,

01:22:00.330 --> 01:22:01.743
and my appreciation for Japanese culture

01:22:01.743 --> 01:22:04.810
and the Japanese language,
came from Japanese TV.

01:22:04.810 --> 01:22:06.980
Like if I wasn't watching anime,

01:22:06.980 --> 01:22:08.162
I was watching, you know--

01:22:08.162 --> 01:22:09.410
- Takeshi's Castle.
- Yeah, Takeshi's Castle.

01:22:09.410 --> 01:22:11.960
- Yeah. We love that, we
talked about it last time.

01:22:12.840 --> 01:22:15.440
- Variety of shows and as I got older,

01:22:15.440 --> 01:22:16.760
and like into my high school years,

01:22:16.760 --> 01:22:18.700
I watch a lot of talk shows.

01:22:18.700 --> 01:22:20.503
Because I was just
genuinely interested in,

01:22:20.503 --> 01:22:22.220
how talk shows work.

01:22:22.220 --> 01:22:24.600
And I started to like growing
appreciation for that.

01:22:24.600 --> 01:22:28.382
But then that entire illusion
just got completely shattered.

01:22:28.382 --> 01:22:31.160
The moment I went onto one of those shows

01:22:31.160 --> 01:22:33.707
and I realized just how
fucking fake that shit is.

01:22:33.707 --> 01:22:36.280
- I feel in general, they're pretty,

01:22:36.280 --> 01:22:39.730
very open about just like, kind
of like softly anti-foreign.

01:22:39.730 --> 01:22:41.800
Like not saying bad
things about foreigners,

01:22:41.800 --> 01:22:43.310
but just like...

01:22:43.310 --> 01:22:45.100
- Yeah, no, you're right.

01:22:45.100 --> 01:22:46.840
- They like to, just saying,

01:22:46.840 --> 01:22:49.065
they do you say pen rather loudly.

01:22:49.065 --> 01:22:51.815
(the rest laugh)

01:22:52.810 --> 01:22:53.720
It's never direct.

01:22:53.720 --> 01:22:55.570
It's just like, we're not
saying there's any difference

01:22:55.570 --> 01:22:57.400
but they just happen to say
the p sound, really loud.

01:22:57.400 --> 01:22:59.560
- Just say the p word.

01:22:59.560 --> 01:23:03.483
- There is undertone.
Nationalistic sectionalism.

01:23:03.483 --> 01:23:05.640
I actually did script a segment on that.

01:23:05.640 --> 01:23:08.340
And I was like, I don't want
to open up Pandora's box.

01:23:11.880 --> 01:23:12.850
- I know what you mean.

01:23:12.850 --> 01:23:13.959
You want to get into that.

01:23:13.959 --> 01:23:16.630
- And I script that, and I talked about,

01:23:16.630 --> 01:23:18.570
I want to keep it funny and on point.

01:23:18.570 --> 01:23:20.940
And that is a dark turn.

01:23:20.940 --> 01:23:21.773
- Yeah.

01:23:21.773 --> 01:23:24.040
- It's a segment now.
- It's an uncomfortable topic.

01:23:24.040 --> 01:23:25.897
Right, people don't like--
- It is, yeah.

01:23:25.897 --> 01:23:26.810
- Absolutely it is there, you know,

01:23:26.810 --> 01:23:29.730
like Japan is special,
right? Japan is better.

01:23:29.730 --> 01:23:31.310
They kind of hinted that

01:23:31.310 --> 01:23:33.420
in the rhetoric of Japanese television.

01:23:33.420 --> 01:23:36.082
And it was like, no, I
don't want to open this box.

01:23:36.082 --> 01:23:37.820
- Yeah.
- It's not worth it.

01:23:37.820 --> 01:23:40.871
- I don't want to--
- So you hate Japan?

01:23:40.871 --> 01:23:44.590
- Yeah, exactly. I'm a
bit scared of this video

01:23:44.590 --> 01:23:46.410
because I think it's the first time

01:23:46.410 --> 01:23:49.330
I've been critical, to some
extent about Japanese culture

01:23:49.330 --> 01:23:51.013
and that's something you just don't do

01:23:51.013 --> 01:23:53.123
because why are you here?

01:23:53.123 --> 01:23:55.260
- Why you even in Japan
if you don't like it.

01:23:55.260 --> 01:23:57.440
- If you don't like it, leave.

01:23:57.440 --> 01:24:00.670
- Do you find like that you
can't really be openly critical

01:24:00.670 --> 01:24:01.900
about Japan on your channel then?

01:24:01.900 --> 01:24:05.030
- I can, but I feel I don't
have that many criticism.

01:24:05.030 --> 01:24:08.510
The thing is I have had very
positive experience in Japan.

01:24:08.510 --> 01:24:11.690
I've never felt, I've suffered any racism,

01:24:11.690 --> 01:24:12.630
in my daily life here,

01:24:12.630 --> 01:24:13.463
in eight years.

01:24:13.463 --> 01:24:15.850
If I had some openly racist,
unpleasant experience.

01:24:15.850 --> 01:24:17.730
Make no mistake, I would comment on that

01:24:17.730 --> 01:24:18.846
and I'll make a video about that.

01:24:18.846 --> 01:24:19.679
And I've been very lucky.

01:24:19.679 --> 01:24:23.050
And my time here has been very positive.

01:24:23.050 --> 01:24:25.908
So I really don't have much to draw from

01:24:25.908 --> 01:24:27.240
in terms of bad experiences.

01:24:27.240 --> 01:24:28.863
If I did, though, I would
be the first to comment on

01:24:28.863 --> 01:24:31.073
- Because we all know, there
are a lot of as J-vloggers

01:24:31.073 --> 01:24:34.433
who are very quick to
like, go on like the whole,

01:24:35.360 --> 01:24:36.883
I experienced a racist thing.

01:24:38.110 --> 01:24:39.760
- Sometimes I kind of wished

01:24:39.760 --> 01:24:40.700
that they would show some restraint

01:24:40.700 --> 01:24:41.990
when they do, because
sometimes you watch it

01:24:41.990 --> 01:24:45.010
and it's like, that wasn't
really worth talking about.

01:24:45.010 --> 01:24:46.000
Like you know what I mean,

01:24:46.000 --> 01:24:49.640
I was like, "they looked at
me funny on the supermarket."

01:24:49.640 --> 01:24:50.720
- Well, I mean, not the train here.

01:24:50.720 --> 01:24:52.110
It was like the busiest train ever.

01:24:52.110 --> 01:24:53.670
But the seat next to me was empty.

01:24:53.670 --> 01:24:54.503
- That's how it is.

01:24:54.503 --> 01:24:55.440
- is that racism?

01:24:55.440 --> 01:24:56.580
- Yeah.
- Debate.

01:24:56.580 --> 01:24:57.960
- I think it was that. Just don't cough,

01:24:57.960 --> 01:25:00.930
if you want to see real
fast, it's rush hour.

01:25:00.930 --> 01:25:03.260
I'm sorry, I can't take any chances.

01:25:03.260 --> 01:25:04.577
- This things are like that.

01:25:04.577 --> 01:25:07.060
But I've never felt like uncomfortable.

01:25:07.060 --> 01:25:08.922
- No, I'm just saying.

01:25:08.922 --> 01:25:09.810
- Which is rare, right?

01:25:09.810 --> 01:25:12.070
Because you don't live in Tokyo.

01:25:12.070 --> 01:25:13.600
- I don't live in Tokyo,
I live in North Japan,

01:25:13.600 --> 01:25:16.250
and I've traveled Japan
extensively, like so much.

01:25:16.250 --> 01:25:18.310
And I very, I honestly can't think

01:25:18.310 --> 01:25:21.450
of an experience where
someone has been openly racist

01:25:21.450 --> 01:25:22.283
towards me or done something

01:25:22.283 --> 01:25:24.400
that made me feel uncomfortable.

01:25:24.400 --> 01:25:25.373
But I've kept an eye out for it.

01:25:25.373 --> 01:25:27.280
Make no mistake.

01:25:27.280 --> 01:25:30.107
- Because people always go (laughs).

01:25:30.107 --> 01:25:32.140
- But people must be
going, is Japan racist,

01:25:32.140 --> 01:25:33.530
you know, what am I going to expect?

01:25:33.530 --> 01:25:35.840
And those bars where
foreigners aren't welcome.

01:25:35.840 --> 01:25:37.460
There are few and far between.

01:25:37.460 --> 01:25:39.330
And they're often in tourist areas,

01:25:39.330 --> 01:25:41.180
where there's a bar that
has regular customers

01:25:41.180 --> 01:25:42.540
and they'd probably just don't want,

01:25:42.540 --> 01:25:43.653
foreign customers coming in.

01:25:43.653 --> 01:25:45.910
Because they can't communicate in.

01:25:45.910 --> 01:25:47.302
- They don't have that respect.

01:25:47.302 --> 01:25:49.160
(laughs)

01:25:49.160 --> 01:25:49.993
- Hitting on that point,

01:25:49.993 --> 01:25:52.150
I watched a video of yours
again last night again,

01:25:52.150 --> 01:25:53.320
I did a deep dive in your channel.

01:25:53.320 --> 01:25:54.903
- You went really deep.

01:25:54.903 --> 01:25:56.897
You are so good at that.

01:25:56.897 --> 01:25:58.300
You read really deep in your research.

01:25:58.300 --> 01:26:01.240
- I did. In 2018 of October,

01:26:01.240 --> 01:26:02.530
you uploaded a video where you were like,

01:26:02.530 --> 01:26:04.270
how long will live in Japan for?

01:26:04.270 --> 01:26:05.570
and in that video you were like,

01:26:05.570 --> 01:26:07.260
maybe like another three years.

01:26:07.260 --> 01:26:08.600
We're getting close to that point, Chris.

01:26:08.600 --> 01:26:11.398
And I was wondering, what are
your thoughts about that now?

01:26:11.398 --> 01:26:13.078
Or is this going to be
something you discuss

01:26:13.078 --> 01:26:13.911
in a video in future?

01:26:13.911 --> 01:26:16.300
- There's still no plans to be honest.

01:26:16.300 --> 01:26:18.240
Before I leave, the one
thing I always want to do

01:26:18.240 --> 01:26:20.983
is to film a short film, to make a film.

01:26:22.174 --> 01:26:23.663
- I think you could pull it off.

01:26:23.663 --> 01:26:25.627
- Everything I've been
doing all these years,

01:26:25.627 --> 01:26:27.300
has been building up to that moment.

01:26:27.300 --> 01:26:28.740
Basically in my free time,

01:26:28.740 --> 01:26:31.090
I've been studying
cinematography and stuff.

01:26:31.090 --> 01:26:33.330
And, that is the one thing I want to do.

01:26:33.330 --> 01:26:35.430
So I feel like once I've done that, maybe.

01:26:36.400 --> 01:26:38.070
- If you did have leave Japan,

01:26:38.070 --> 01:26:39.320
how do you think, like that, I mean

01:26:39.320 --> 01:26:40.530
how would it affect your channel?

01:26:40.530 --> 01:26:42.176
- It's Abroad in the UK.

01:26:42.176 --> 01:26:43.863
(laugh)

01:26:43.863 --> 01:26:46.360
- It would just be Abroad.

01:26:46.360 --> 01:26:47.540
- Do you almost feel at times that,

01:26:47.540 --> 01:26:49.900
maybe you're like hostage to Japan.

01:26:49.900 --> 01:26:53.170
But you're kind of like,
well, my job is Japan.

01:26:53.170 --> 01:26:54.164
Like, can I leave?

01:26:54.164 --> 01:26:58.633
- Not really. You think so,
but not necessarily, no.

01:27:00.150 --> 01:27:01.570
I mean, my channel is, let's face it

01:27:01.570 --> 01:27:03.005
the reason the channel is so successful is

01:27:03.005 --> 01:27:04.960
because most of my viewers
are interested in Japan.

01:27:04.960 --> 01:27:05.793
- Right.

01:27:05.793 --> 01:27:07.030
- And I'm fine with that.

01:27:07.030 --> 01:27:09.260
I do have a second channel
called Abroad Perspective.

01:27:09.260 --> 01:27:10.093
- Right.
- Right.

01:27:10.093 --> 01:27:10.970
- Clever (laughs).

01:27:12.510 --> 01:27:13.707
- You upload a lot of videos, where

01:27:13.707 --> 01:27:16.027
you just chat shit to the
comments that you get, right?

01:27:16.027 --> 01:27:17.383
And it's fantastic.

01:27:18.714 --> 01:27:21.376
- Are they replying-to-hate
comments video?

01:27:21.376 --> 01:27:23.640
- You have a lot of videos where you just,

01:27:23.640 --> 01:27:26.110
reply to comments and those get
just as many views sometimes

01:27:26.110 --> 01:27:27.120
as you, maybe.
- They do.

01:27:27.120 --> 01:27:28.700
- So I feel like, even if you did leave,

01:27:28.700 --> 01:27:30.010
you could easily transition.

01:27:30.010 --> 01:27:31.987
- Yeah. I do think if
I had to leave Japan,

01:27:31.987 --> 01:27:33.220
and go for a bit, there would be a future.

01:27:33.220 --> 01:27:34.501
I would be able to do something.

01:27:34.501 --> 01:27:35.610
I would be able to pivot,

01:27:35.610 --> 01:27:37.780
and create a channel
that's focused on comedy

01:27:37.780 --> 01:27:38.727
or commentating or something.

01:27:38.727 --> 01:27:41.450
But really I've always
seen my YouTube channel,

01:27:41.450 --> 01:27:44.190
as a YouTube channel and
also have a stepping stone

01:27:45.598 --> 01:27:47.670
to getting into the film industry.

01:27:47.670 --> 01:27:48.572
And in the world of film.

01:27:48.572 --> 01:27:49.563
- So is that like your
ultimate goal after YouTube?

01:27:49.563 --> 01:27:52.790
- That is my ultimate goal,
and 2020 is supposed to be,

01:27:52.790 --> 01:27:54.735
or supposed to be the
year that I did that.

01:27:54.735 --> 01:27:55.568
- Okay.

01:27:56.693 --> 01:27:58.060
- That's going to be kind
of been a bit delayed

01:27:59.280 --> 01:28:00.740
Given what's going on.

01:28:00.740 --> 01:28:01.960
- Things move slowly, right?

01:28:01.960 --> 01:28:03.190
- Yeah.

01:28:03.190 --> 01:28:04.600
- So you have like no interest

01:28:04.600 --> 01:28:06.933
in staying for the foreseeable future?

01:28:08.242 --> 01:28:11.763
- I think I'll be here at
least another three years.

01:28:12.755 --> 01:28:14.380
I don't have a like, it's time to go now.

01:28:14.380 --> 01:28:16.150
End goal, like I have to leave Japan like.

01:28:16.150 --> 01:28:18.040
- I didn't say three years (laughs).

01:28:18.040 --> 01:28:19.810
- More realistically,
I'll probably be here

01:28:19.810 --> 01:28:20.643
permanently another few years,

01:28:20.643 --> 01:28:22.650
and then maybe I'll transition to the UK

01:28:22.650 --> 01:28:23.740
and I'll come back to Japan.

01:28:23.740 --> 01:28:26.011
- Could you see yourself,
like if you did stay in Japan.

01:28:26.011 --> 01:28:30.330
Like you've done so much
content in and around Japan.

01:28:30.330 --> 01:28:33.060
Could you ever see yourself
at a point where it's like,

01:28:33.060 --> 01:28:36.070
I've literally run out of every
idea that I could think of.

01:28:36.070 --> 01:28:37.610
That's like interesting enough in Japan,

01:28:37.610 --> 01:28:39.220
because you know like,

01:28:39.220 --> 01:28:40.820
- You think so?
- As diverse,

01:28:40.820 --> 01:28:45.120
and as like interesting as all
sorts of places in Japan are,

01:28:45.120 --> 01:28:47.300
if you cover also all
the interesting stuff,

01:28:47.300 --> 01:28:49.420
eventually you think you're
gonna run out, right?

01:28:49.420 --> 01:28:51.130
So like, could you ever see yourself,

01:28:51.130 --> 01:28:52.220
like getting to that point?

01:28:52.220 --> 01:28:54.850
Or would you probably
bail before that happens?

01:28:54.850 --> 01:28:55.750
- That's a good question.

01:28:55.750 --> 01:28:56.583
People ask that a lot.

01:28:56.583 --> 01:28:57.740
Like are you fed up of covering Japan?

01:28:57.740 --> 01:28:59.220
And I think there's always a new angle,

01:28:59.220 --> 01:29:00.250
a new story to be found,

01:29:00.250 --> 01:29:02.330
like recently I've working on a series

01:29:02.330 --> 01:29:04.220
about business owners in Japan.

01:29:04.220 --> 01:29:05.830
So I made a series about

01:29:05.830 --> 01:29:07.510
a guy that owns a sushi restaurant

01:29:07.510 --> 01:29:09.700
and what's it like and he's a
good friend of mine in Sendai.

01:29:09.700 --> 01:29:11.940
He owns the biggest sushi
restaurant chain in Sendai.

01:29:11.940 --> 01:29:14.380
I've got another friend who
owns a Wagyu restaurant.

01:29:14.380 --> 01:29:15.649
And I've been chatting with him,

01:29:15.649 --> 01:29:16.910
and we're going to make a video on that.

01:29:16.910 --> 01:29:18.960
So focusing on people is
another option, right.

01:29:18.960 --> 01:29:20.170
I've never really done that.

01:29:20.170 --> 01:29:21.460
And it's something I've
always wanted to do.

01:29:21.460 --> 01:29:23.730
So focusing on different people.

01:29:23.730 --> 01:29:25.220
So I always think there's another angle.

01:29:25.220 --> 01:29:26.290
There's another story to be told.

01:29:26.290 --> 01:29:29.790
I don't think, you know,
I've got 20, 30, 40 ideas

01:29:29.790 --> 01:29:30.623
in the back of my mind

01:29:30.623 --> 01:29:32.260
or written down a document that I can go.

01:29:32.260 --> 01:29:34.850
So there's no absence of content.

01:29:34.850 --> 01:29:36.280
- Because I feel like as a YouTuber,

01:29:36.280 --> 01:29:37.440
especially if you're on the platform

01:29:37.440 --> 01:29:39.450
for like a very long time, you eventually,

01:29:39.450 --> 01:29:41.980
have to think about evolving
your content, right?

01:29:41.980 --> 01:29:42.813
- Right.

01:29:42.813 --> 01:29:45.285
- Because like anyone,
like if you pay attention

01:29:45.285 --> 01:29:47.360
to the world of YouTube,
anyone who's successful in here

01:29:47.360 --> 01:29:49.330
or has been for a very long time,

01:29:49.330 --> 01:29:50.700
their content has to like

01:29:50.700 --> 01:29:51.990
slowly change over time,

01:29:51.990 --> 01:29:54.100
or you have to try to explore new things.

01:29:54.100 --> 01:29:55.516
And I feel like one of
the biggest challenges,

01:29:55.516 --> 01:29:56.890
is trying to figure out,

01:29:56.890 --> 01:29:58.750
what you can kind of get away with.

01:29:58.750 --> 01:30:03.750
Because what I fear most
is getting pigeonholed

01:30:04.300 --> 01:30:05.853
into like one type of content.

01:30:07.210 --> 01:30:08.093
I love anime.

01:30:09.470 --> 01:30:11.930
But have you ever felt
you wanted to make content

01:30:11.930 --> 01:30:14.320
outside of anime or like
something that's not

01:30:14.320 --> 01:30:15.840
about Japan itself.

01:30:15.840 --> 01:30:19.040
- I mean, that's like what
this podcast is for us.

01:30:19.040 --> 01:30:21.030
I can finally talk about shit that's not

01:30:21.030 --> 01:30:23.200
specifically about anime.

01:30:23.200 --> 01:30:27.580
Because I do have, so many
other like interesting things

